              |___/|_|                

[build output...]
webpack built 8a2f3e1c2d4b5a6f in 45231ms
[INFO] Server running at http://calypso.localhost:3000

Ready! You can load http://calypso.localhost:3000/ now. Have fun!
```

The server successfully started on port 3000 as configured, and the cyan-colored "Ready!" message appeared once webpack finished compiling all assets.

Next I wanted to understand how to know when the server is fully ready. I searched for the ready message:

```bash
grep -n "Ready\!" client/server/bundler/index.js
```

Output:

```
56:							`\nReady! You can load ${ protocol }://${ host }:${ port }/ now. Have fun!`
60:					console.info( chalk.cyan( '\nReady! All assets are re-compiled. Have fun!' ) );
72:			`Compiling assets... Wait until you see Ready! and then try ${ protocol }://${ host }:${ port }/ again.`
```

I extracted the exact console.info statements:

```bash
sed -n '54,62p' client/server/bundler/index.js
```

Output:

```
				console.info(
					chalk.cyan(
						`\nReady! You can load ${ protocol }://${ host }:${ port }/ now. Have fun!`
					)
				);
			} else {
				console.info( chalk.cyan( '\nReady! All assets are re-compiled. Have fun!' ) );
			}
		} );
```

The relevant code in `client/server/bundler/index.js` (lines 38-64) shows webpack's done hook:

```javascript
compiler.hooks.done.tap( 'Calypso', function () {
    built = true;
    // ...
    process.nextTick( function () {
        process.nextTick( function () {
            if ( beforeFirstCompile ) {
                beforeFirstCompile = false;
                console.info(
                    chalk.cyan(
                        `\nReady! You can load ${ protocol }://${ host }:${ port }/ now. Have fun!`
                    )
                );
            } else {
                console.info( chalk.cyan( '\nReady! All assets are re-compiled. Have fun!' ) );
            }
        } );
    } );
} );
```

The server is ready when you see the cyan-colored message "Ready! You can load http://calypso.localhost:3000/ now. Have fun!" in the terminal. On subsequent recompilations, it shows "Ready! All assets are re-compiled. Have fun!"

I then investigated whether the architecture uses multiple ports for hot reloading and API calls, or if everything is served from one place. I searched for separate port configurations:

```bash
grep -rn "HMR_PORT\|DEV_PORT\|HOT_PORT" client/server/
```

The command returned no output, meaning no separate port configurations were found.

I checked the middleware setup:

```bash
sed -n '100,102p' client/server/bundler/index.js
```

Output:

```
	app.use( waitForCompiler );
	app.use( webpackMiddleware( compiler ) );
	app.use( hotMiddleware( compiler ) );
```

And verified the middleware imports:

```bash
grep -n "webpack-dev-middleware\|webpack-hot-middleware" client/server/bundler/index.js
```

Output:

```
5:const webpackMiddleware = require( 'webpack-dev-middleware' );
6:const hotMiddleware = require( 'webpack-hot-middleware' );
```

Everything is served from a single port (3000). Hot module reloading uses webpack-hot-middleware which communicates via Server-Sent Events at /__webpack_hmr on the same port, not a separate WebSocket port.

